            <ArticleTitle>Spigelian hernia presenting as an appendicular mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1037-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Incarcerated spigelian hernias are a rare cause of acute abdomen. The clinical diagnosis of incarcerated spigelian hernia can be a challenge in the absence of definite signs. Reported here is a case of a strangulated spigelian hernia that mimicked an appendicular mass and was discovered on CT scan of the abdomen and pelvis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
